WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.427
A filtered view introduces an important write question.

00:00:03.427 --> 00:00:10.457
If the view only shows active patients, what should happen when an update through the view sets active

00:00:10.457 --> 00:00:15.767
to false? Without a check option, the row may simply disappear from the view after the update.

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:20.897
WITH CHECK OPTION can enforce the view condition for writes performed through the view.

00:00:20.897 --> 00:00:26.297
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:26.297 --> 00:00:33.162
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:33.162 --> 00:00:39.600
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
